  "The natural {en:vironment:Surroundings or conditions in which living organisms reside.} is vital for global biodiversity. Conserving native {ha:bitats:Natural homes of animals or plants.} ensures the survival of endangered species. Pollution severely damages {aq:uatic:Relating to water ecosystems.} ecosystems and reduces freshwater quality. Sustainable farming practices protect soil {fe:rtility:Ability of soil to sustain agricultural plant growth.} and reduce chemical runoff. Every community must participate in environmental {pr:eservation:Act of keeping something safe and undamaged.}.",
