  "Artificial satellites orbit Earth in designated orbital tracks. Telecommunication satellites transmit television, internet, and radio {si:gnals:Gestures, actions, or sounds conveying information.}. Weather satellites monitor hurricane development and atmospheric pressure changes. Space debris poses a collision hazard to active orbital spacecraft. Engineers design orbital cleanup systems to mitigate space clutter.",
  "The human circulatory system transports oxygen and essential {nu:trients:Substances supplying nourishment for growth.} through blood vessels. The heart pumps oxygenated blood through arteries to body tissues. Red blood cells contain hemoglobin, which binds oxygen {mo:lecules:Groups of atoms bonded together.}. Proper physical exercise strengthens cardiovascular muscles and boosts stamina. Maintaining healthy blood pressure reduces the risk of heart disease.",
  "The central nervous system consists of the brain and spinal {co:rd:Long thin structure carrying nerve impulses.}. Neurons transmit electrical signals across synaptic gaps to process information. Sensory organs detect environmental stimuli and convey signals to the cerebral {co:rtex:Outer layer of neural tissue in the brain.}. Regular physical rest and mental stimulation optimize neural cognitive functions. Healthy sleep cycles consolidate memory pathways.",
  "Human digestion breaks down food into simple chemical compounds. The stomach uses gastric acids and enzymes to dissolve dietary {pr:oteins:Complex organic macromolecules essential for life.}. Small intestines absorb vital vitamins, minerals, and glucose into the bloodstream. Dietary fiber promotes beneficial intestinal bacterial flora and smooth digestion. Balanced nutrition prevents metabolic disorders.",
  "The human immune system protects the body against invading pathogenic {mi:crobes:Microscopic organisms causing disease.}. White blood cells produce specialized antibodies to neutralize foreign antigens. Immunization trains the immune system to recognize specific viral strains quickly. Maintaining good personal hygiene minimizes exposure to infectious agents. Adequate hydration and nutrition support immune response.",
  "Respiratory organs facilitate gas exchange between blood and the external atmosphere. Lungs absorb oxygen and eliminate carbon dioxide during cellular {re:spiration:Process of inhaling oxygen and exhaling carbon dioxide.}. Respiratory cilia filter dust particles and pollutants from inhaled air. Clean air environments protect pulmonary tissues from chronic inflammation. Regular exercise expands lung capacity and oxygen intake.",
  "Ancient agricultural civilizations flourished near fertile river valley {re:gions:Extensive geographic areas.}. Farmers constructed irrigation networks to divert river water to cropland. Surplus food production allowed communities to develop urban centers and specialized {tr:ades:Occupations requiring manual or mechanical skill.}. Written scripts emerged to record commercial transactions and legal codes. Agriculture established the foundation of organized societies.",
  "The invention of the printing press transformed European literacy and information {di:ssemination:Act of spreading something widely.}. Bound books became affordable and accessible to wider social classes. Scientific treatises and philosophical ideas spread rapidly across international borders. Standardized print encouraged national language development and educational reform. Mass printing accelerated the intellectual progress of the Enlightenment.",
  "Maritime trade routes connected ancient empires across vast oceanic distances. Merchant vessels transported spices, silk, ceramics, and precious {me:tals:Solid material that is typically hard and shiny.}. Cultural exchange accompanied commercial trade, sharing artistic styles and ideas. Coastal port cities grew into wealthy cosmopolitan centers of international commerce. Maritime navigation required accurate charts and astronomical tracking.",
  "The Industrial Revolution introduced mechanized manufacturing powered by steam {en:gines:Machines with moving parts that convert power into motion.}. Factories replaced traditional handcraft workshops, increasing output speed dramatically. Railroad networks transported raw materials and manufactured goods across continents. Urban populations expanded rapidly as agricultural workers moved toward industrial cities. Technological innovation reshaped economic structures.",
